# ── PROJECT IDENTITY ────────────────────────────────────────

You are an expert React 18 + Vite engineer building "The Defense Panel" — a real-time AI simulation platform where hyper-realistic Beyond Presence avatars interrogate users on their uploaded presentation documents.

The stack is: React 18 (Vite), Tailwind CSS, Vercel Serverless Functions, OpenAI GPT-4o, Beyond Presence SDK (@bey-dev/sdk), Supabase (PostgreSQL).

This is a 24-hour hackathon build. Every decision must prioritize WORKING DEMO over perfect architecture.

# ── FRAMEWORK RULES ─────────────────────────────────────────

- ALWAYS use React 18 with Vite. NEVER use Next.js, App Router, or server components.
- ALWAYS use functional components with hooks (useState, useRef, useEffect, useContext).
- NEVER use class components.
- NEVER use Redux. State management is React Context API only.
- NEVER use Prisma or any ORM. Use @supabase/supabase-js query builder directly.
- NEVER use Express.js or custom servers. All backend logic lives in /api as Vercel Serverless Functions.
- Keep every component under 200 lines. If it exceeds this, split it.

