# ── AGENT PIPELINE ──────────────────────────────────────────

This is the core innovation. Two agents work in sequence:

AGENT 1 — /api/process-document (GPT-4o)
  Input:  raw PDF text
  Output: { sme_system_prompt, evaluator_system_prompt }
  
  GPT-4o reads the document and GENERATES both system prompts dynamically.
  The SME prompt contains the actual weak claims and tech stack from the PDF.
  The Evaluator prompt contains delivery monitoring instructions.
  Both prompts must be under 800 characters to fit Beyond Presence field limits.

AGENT 2 — /api/start-session (Beyond Presence API)
  Input:  { sme_system_prompt, evaluator_system_prompt }
  Output: { sme_agent_id, evaluator_agent_id }
  
  Creates TWO Beyond Presence agents in parallel using Promise.all.
  Each agent gets its system prompt injected at creation time.
  Both agents are disposable — delete them in /api/end-session.
  Return both agent IDs to the frontend for iframe embedding.

# ── API ROUTE TEMPLATES ─────────────────────────────────────

/api/process-document.js:
  - Method: POST
  - Body: { pdfText: string }
  - Calls GPT-4o with this exact instruction:
    "Read this document. Output ONLY a JSON object with two keys:
     sme_system_prompt (skeptical VC who challenges the exact weak claims in this doc, under 800 chars)
     evaluator_system_prompt (speech coach tracking filler words and pacing, under 800 chars)"
  - Returns: { success: true, prompts: { sme_system_prompt, evaluator_system_prompt } }
  - On error: { success: false, error: "Document processing failed" }

/api/start-session.js:
  - Method: POST  
  - Body: { sme_system_prompt, evaluator_system_prompt }
  - Calls POST https://api.bey.dev/v1/agents TWICE in parallel (Promise.all)
  - Returns: { success: true, sme_agent_id, evaluator_agent_id }
  - On error: { success: false, error: "Agent creation failed" }

/api/end-session.js:
  - Method: POST
  - Body: { transcript, sme_agent_id, evaluator_agent_id, scenario, duration_seconds }
  - Calls GPT-4o to grade the transcript → { filler_word_count, pacing_score, overall_score, critical_feedback }
  - Deletes both Beyond Presence agents (fire and forget)
  - Inserts into Supabase pitch_sessions table
  - Returns: { success: true, grades }

