# ── RISK MITIGATIONS ─────────────────────────────────────────

Risk 1 — Wi-Fi drops during demo:
  Record a flawless 2-minute screen capture video before Hour 10.
  Store locally on presenter's laptop. Play immediately if live demo fails.

Risk 2 — OpenAI rate limits:
  Use hardcoded mock responses during all development and testing.
  Only switch to live OpenAI at final end-to-end test (Hour 9).

Risk 3 — Beyond Presence latency:
  Keep system prompts under 800 characters.
  Use the fastest avatar model available in the dashboard.

Risk 4 — Vercel build crash:
  Never push untested code in the last hour.
  Always rollback via dashboard — never fix under pressure.

Risk 5 — Audio echo in demo:
  Presenter MUST use headphones during live demo.
  Test audio with headphones at Hour 9, not during the presentation.

# ── HACKATHON DEMO SCRIPT ────────────────────────────────────

The 5-minute pitch ends with exactly 1 minute of live demo.
The demo must show:
  1. Upload a PDF pitch deck (pre-loaded for speed)
  2. Click "Initialize Panel" — show the loading overlay
  3. Arena opens — two avatars visible
  4. Presenter speaks and deliberately rambles
  5. SME avatar interrupts: "Stop there. Your PDF says X but you just claimed Y. Explain."
  6. Crowd reacts. Game over. You win.

